{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Disk measurement, 2026-09-05 ~08:30 UTC — evidence for the remaining caps (S3/S4/S5).\n\nCorrecting my own probe first: my initial CloudWatch query returned \"no datapoints\" for every metric and I nearly read that as a dead probe. It was my error twice over — the namespace is lowercase `rebar/host` (I queried `Rebar/Host`; namespaces are case-sensitive), and the returned timestamps carry a `-07:00` offset, so my hour-slice was reading local-offset rather than UTC. With both corrected, five of six metrics ARE publishing currently. Only `var_tmp_used_percent` is genuinely absent.\n\nMeasured, namespace `rebar/host`:\n\n- `docker_unaccounted_bytes` — 2.03 GB (08:19 UTC) -> 2.86 -> 3.02 -> 3.02 -> **3.79 GB (08:29 UTC)**. Threshold is 2 GiB. The scheduled `systemctl restart docker` at 05:23 UTC had brought this to 1.42 GB, so this is ~2.4 GB of regrowth in roughly three hours, and it is still climbing.\n- `docker_buildkit_cache_used_percent` — 99-100% sustained across the whole window, against the 5 GiB BuildKit budget.\n\nThe pair is the informative part. BuildKit sitting pinned at ~100% of its budget is the cap DOING its job — that number is bounded because `builder.gc` is in effect (confirmed earlier by ordering: daemon.json written 01:01 UTC, dockerd ActiveEnterTimestamp 05:23:33 UTC). The unaccounted bytes are the part NOT under any cap, and they are the ones growing. So the storage growth is escaping through the space the container-layer and scratch caps (S3/S5) are meant to close, not through the BuildKit budget already installed by S0/S6.\n\nTwo alarm states here are known-pending and are NOT new findings:\n- `var_tmp_cleanup_active` = 0 across all 33 datapoints. Genuine breach, expected: S4's terraform alarms were applied, but the host-side cleanup unit ships in `user_data`, and the `aws_instance.gerrit` update that installs it was deliberately declined tonight because it requires a Gerrit stop/start. `var_tmp_used_percent` publishing nothing has the same single cause.\n- `gate_scratch_mounted` = 0 across all 33 datapoints. This is dcc3 — the volume is attached but raw/unmounted, and mounting it hides ~9.3 GB of live data, so it needs a quiet window.\n\nNot filing a bug for the docker regrowth: it is this epic's subject, and a separate ticket would duplicate S3/S5 rather than add anything. Recording it here as a measured baseline the remaining stories can be judged against."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788597348892635429,"uuid":"711dfba3-295c-4cb9-83ef-29c2abd93c15"}